{
  "solution": [<selected_item>, <selected_item>, ...]
}

Here "solution" is just the list of the m songs you picked — put each song’s identifier exactly as it appears in the instance (that is, the labels from the song list). Think of this JSON as a simple form: the key is the field name and the array is where you list the selected tracks. This is only a sketch of the expected shape, not the actual answer.

Please use the identifiers exactly as given in the input — no renaming and no new labels.  
Valid identifiers look like plain numbers such as “1” or “23”, single capital letters like “A” or “B”, or a capital letter followed by digits like “A1” or “X7”.

