I'll just show the shape of the output we want — a tiny JSON with the chosen creatives listed inside. Nothing fancy, just put the selected creative identifiers in the array.

{
  "solution": [<selected_item>, <selected_item>, ...]
}

"solution" is the list where you drop the exact identifiers of the creatives you picked (one identifier per selected creative). This JSON is just a sketch of the expected shape — not the final answer itself.

All identifiers must be used exactly as they appear in the instance input — no renaming and no new labels.
- for example: "Valid identifiers look like plain numbers such as “1” or “23”, single capital letters like “A” or “B”, or a capital letter followed by digits like “A1” or “X7”."

At the newsroom meeting the brief was short: assemble exactly the requested number of headline drafts, no repeats, and cover as many distinct tones and angles as possible. The tidy way to score a lineup is to measure how different each pair of drafts is and then add up those pairwise differences — the best collection is the one with the largest combined difference. The exact list of drafts and the number to pick follow below.

